		"summary": "Meteorologists at NOAA’s Climate Prediction Center and Environment and Climate Change Canada are closely tracking sea-surface temperature anomalies across the equatorial Pacific Ocean as the El Niño–Southern Oscillation (ENSO) cycle dictates the 2026–2027 North American winter outlook. Understanding the contrast between El Niño (warmer Pacific waters that split the jet stream and bring wet southern storms) and La Niña (cooler Pacific waters that push the polar jet stream across the Pacific Northwest, Great Lakes, and Canada) is essential for predicting snowfall, ski season totals, and heating costs.",
