					"body": "Once your edited keyframes look photorealistic, bring your original video and your edited keyframes into an **AI Video-to-Video (V2V) engine** that supports **First-Frame / Structure Reference**: **Runway Gen-3 Alpha (Video-to-Video with First Frame guide)**, **Kling AI 1.6**, **Pika (Pikaffects / Pikaswaps)**, or the open-source **ComfyUI + Wan 2.1 VACE / ControlNet Depth + Pose** pipeline. Split your 23-second video into **3-to-5-second cuts** at natural camera pans (00:00–00:06 getting out of the Lambo, 00:06–00:13 walking toward the tree and pointing at the red Ferrari SF90, and 00:13–00:23 showing the watches). Using **Depth ControlNet + DWPose**, the AI wraps the tailored brown suit around your torso and arms with realistic fabric folds while anchoring the red Ferrari SF90 to the lawn behind you."
