					"body": "The #1 giveaway of amateur AI video is a 'melting' face or out-of-sync mouth when the creator speaks. Notice how in the viral clip, the creator's face, curly hair, and lip movements in the top ('AI') panel are **100% identical** to the bottom ('Original') panel! You achieve this in post-production (After Effects, DaVinci Resolve, or CapCut) by **rotoscoping/masking your original real head and neck** from the raw footage and compositing it right back on top of the AI-suited body (matching skin color temperature slightly). Finally, keep the **original microphone audio track** from your real recording so your voice, breathing, and lip-sync remain 100% authentic."
